    <briefdescription>
<para>Attach the radio&apos;s configured link graph before reading peer audio. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Call on the control plane before starting the peer reader. The caller retains the peer channel until this synchronous call returns; the peer datastore then owns the hook. Disabled processing retains the profile for later reloads. Repeating the same binding is harmless; rebinding to another profile fails. Require both a zero return and the accepted ABI: Asterisk can return success for options unknown to an older driver. No public loader ABI changes. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
